<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baia is a village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suceava">Suceava</a> County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, and one of the oldest towns of Moldavia, with an early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> community and a Catholic church. In December 1467 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-the-great">Stephen the Great</a> defeated the invading Hungarian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a> there, ending Hungarian attempts to subdue Moldavia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baia-romania.jpg" alt="Baia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cezar Suceveanu · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Biserica_Alba_din_Baia9.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
